{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1433324-temporis-vs-time-sphere-debacle","id":1433324,"title":"Temporis vs time sphere debacle","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-01-24T15:59:56-08:00","id":1433324,"title":"Temporis vs time sphere debacle","content":"I have a campaign that I'm writing for that players veto'd mage since its super complicated. But short and sweet I got a new batch of players so I can add mage shennanigens in my multi supernatural world i've created.<br /> <br /> A major plot in the matter is that the setting is influenced heavy by a massive time loop. Deja vu runs rampant. People are misbehaving and acting amiss (cause they should be dead but arent). Etc etc.<br /> <br /> I had a player wanting to play a true brujah vampire with temporis. As you know he would start being able to sense time dilations so his spidey sense should ideally go off 24/7. But how would you compare time sphere magic against temporis if the situation ever comes into play?<br /> <br /> Other supernatural time manipulation factors are in play too. So feel free to describe those as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19533-pnizzle","name":"Pnizzle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-24T16:24:06-08:00","id":1433327,"title":"","content":"As with all Spheres, Time begins with sensory effects. A mage with Time 1 should also be getting the sense that something's wrong with the flow of time, though it might take a ritual effect (that is, a bunch of successes) to determine just what's going wrong. <br /> <br /> Actually <i>manipulating</i> the flow of time requires more dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-25T10:52:57-08:00","id":1433411,"title":"","content":"Indeed. Essentially *having* Time 1 would allow the Mage to sense that &quot;something is going on&quot;. Just that vibe nagging at the back of their head, probably causing repeated perception + awareness (not alertness) rolls over time. Without really needing to see a Deja Vu or anything themselves.<br /> <br /> Then, an actual roll of Arete using Time 1 might net a few successes and they'd probably see time getting distorted - a confirmation of their earlier suspicions. But a couple of successes with that big of an effect going on would be akin to suddenly being able to see air move while being inside a hurricane.<br /> <br /> To get the overall picture, as Dataweaver said, they'd probably need a pile of successes - and even then, depending on the complexity of what's going on, gaining really good insight of what's happening at the place they are at might not give a complete overall picture yet.<br /> <br /> <br /> Time 2 then would allow them to see into the past and future (the latter to a certain unreliable degree...). Or, in this case, they might use it to see how time at a spot was distorted (or non-distorted) in the past, and how it *might* be distorted in the future.<br /> <br /> Time 3 would allow the Mage to stretch/speed up and condense/slow down time around them (or roll it back a couple turns) - maybe at least temporarily trying to slow or speed up the effects of whatever is going on where they're at, but it's not until Time 4 or 5 where the Mage would be able to possibly permanently normalize things again at a location or as a whole - but possibly not without some serious investigation into the matter.<br /> <br /> Ultimately it might be easier to remove the source than fight the symptom either way, and I have a feeling that's where your campaign is heading <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 01-25-2021, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}